{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open closed principle open closed principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","fileName":"Open-Closed Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Open-Closed Principle","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Software Design Principles]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open closed principle open closed principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","fileName":"Open-Closed Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Open-Closed Principle","heading":"Open-Closed Principle","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The open-closed principle favors extending behavior through a defined contract while keeping established client-facing behavior stable. A caller that depends on an interface can accept a new implementation without rewriting the caller for each variant. The useful boundary is the one likely to vary; adding an interface for every class before variation appears can make the design more complex without improving extensibility.\n\nThe principle favors adding behavior through extension points over repeatedly editing stable classes, modules, or functions. Its purpose is to reduce regression risk, but the extension mechanism must still reflect a variation the software genuinely needs.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open closed principle open closed principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Open-Closed Principle.md","fileName":"Open-Closed Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Open-Closed Principle","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}